 ntroduces SecureMyFutureResearch\, a course designed to help graduate-lev
 el researchers anticipate these requirements before they create delays\, 
 uncertainty\, or risks to research data. Participants will receive an ove
 rview of the course's six-stage research lifecycle roadmap\, from develop
 ing a project and obtaining approvals through data collection\, retention
 \, sharing\, and destruction.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;1342331
 17&quot\;:false\,&quot\;134233118&quot\;:false\,&quot\;335559738&quot\;:2
 40\,&quot\;335559739&quot\;:0}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="none">
 __________</span></p><p>  New to research\, new to managing your own data
 \, or interested in learning more about research data support at IU? Over
  the course of the Fall 2026 semester\, join us for webinars designed to 
 walk you through the basics of researching with data at IU— from organi
 zing and storing your data to meeting funder requirements and finding the
  right tools.</p><p>  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the IU Research Data Commo
 ns\, and other campus partners\, with sessions useful for researchers at 
 any stage. Some sessions may require advanced registration.</p><p>  For a
 ny questions\, please contact the IU Libraries Research Data Services tea
