DESCRIPTION:While incredibly powerful\, it requires a significant amount 
 of time and preparation to be done well. Attendees of this webinar will l
 earn best practices for preparing for Evidence Synthesis (which includes 
 Systematic Reviews\, Scoping Reviews\, Umbrella Reviews\, etc.)\, and the
  tools and support available to IU researchers.__________  New to researc
 h\, new to managing your own data\, or interested in learning more about 
 research data support at IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 semester\, 
 join us for webinars designed to walk you through the basics of researchi
 ng with data at IU— from organizing and storing your data to meeting fu
 nder requirements and finding the right tools.  Hosted by IU Libraries\, 
 the IU Research Data Commons\, and other campus partners\, with sessions 
 useful for researchers at any stage. Some sessions may require advanced r
 egistration.  For any questions\, please contact the IU Libraries Researc
 h Data Services team (resdata@iu.edu (mailto:resdata@iu.edu)) - and don't
  forget to check back regularly\, as new sessions are added!
