DTSTART:20261002T180000Z
DTEND:20261002T193000Z
LOCATION:Hamilton Lugar School of Global and International Studies
GEO:39.170011;-86.517418
SUMMARY:Lecture: "Lessons from a Rapid-Response Web-Archiving Effort" wit
 h Anna Kijas
DESCRIPTION:Anna E. Kijas is Assistant Director of Digital Scholarship an
 d Lilly Music Library at Tufts University. She co-founded Saving Ukrainia
 n Cultural Heritage Online\, an initiative focused on safeguarding and pr
 eserving the digital cultural heritage of Ukraine during the Russo-Ukrain
 ian War.  Anna's work is centered on principles of social justice\, acces
 s\, and sustainability in relation to digital humanities\, historical (mu
 sic) research\, cultural heritage\, and information studies. Her recent p
 ublications include a special issue\, "Cultural Heritage in Crisis\," for
  the journal Library Trends\, a co-authored chapter\, "Nimble Tents and B
 unkers: The Role of Libraries in Rapid-Response DH\," in The Routledge Co
 mpanion to Libraries\, Archives\, and the Digital Humanities\, a book ent
 itled The Life and Music of Teresa Carreño (1853-1917): A Guide to Resea
 rch\, and open-access digital projects\, including Documenting Teresa Car
 reño and Rebalancing the Music Canon.  Cosponsored by The Byrnes Institu
 te (REEI)\, IU Libraries\, and The Department of Information and Library 
 Science.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Anna E. Kijas is Assistant Director of 
 Digital Scholarship and Lilly Music Library at Tufts University. She co-f
 ounded Saving Ukrainian Cultural Heritage Online\, an initiative focused 
 on safeguarding and preserving the digital cultural heritage of Ukraine d
 uring the Russo-Ukrainian War.</p><p>  Anna's work is centered on princip
 les of social justice\, access\, and sustainability in relation to digita
 l humanities\, historical (music) research\, cultural heritage\, and info
 rmation studies. Her recent publications include a special issue\, "Cultu
 ral Heritage in Crisis\," for the journal Library Trends\, a co-authored 
 chapter\, "Nimble Tents and Bunkers: The Role of Libraries in Rapid-Respo
 nse DH\," in The Routledge Companion to Libraries\, Archives\, and the Di
 gital Humanities\, a book entitled The Life and Music of Teresa Carreño 
 (1853-1917): A Guide to Research\, and open-access digital projects\, inc
 luding Documenting Teresa Carreño and Rebalancing the Music Canon.</p><p
 >  Cosponsored by The Byrnes Institute (REEI)\, IU Libraries\, and The De
 partment of Information and Library Science.</p>
UID:20261002T180000Z-2428178@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20260923T145730Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2428178-lecture-lessons-from-a-
 rapid-response-web-archiving-
CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
LAST-MODIFIED:20260925T150238Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop
 /1/src_region/0,0,501,498/32679_kijas.rev.1790191504.png
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2428178
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/heig
 ht/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,501\,498/32679_kijas.rev.1790191504.png
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  Laikin Dantchenko\, <a href="mailto:ldant
 ch@iu.edu">ldantch@iu.edu</a>&#160\;\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>Anna Kijas\, co-founder of Saving Ukrainian Cultur
 al Heritage Online (SUCHO)\, will discuss this rapid-response web-archivi
 ng effort\, how it drew together a community of activists\, and what the 
 global cultural heritage community can learn from the invasion of Ukraine
  to plan for more resilient futures for digital cultural heritage protect
 ion.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TAGS:archives|Arts and Humanities|cultural heritage|Digital H
 umanities|digital scholarship|music history|Music Library|Ukraine
END:VEVENT
