SUMMARY:The Cost of Value(s): What Should Libraries Pay For?
DESCRIPTION:Every subscription renewed\, publishing agreement signed\, in
 frastructure project supported\, or service discontinued helps shape the 
 scholarly communication ecosystem—for better or for worse.  But making 
 spending decisions that reflect library values is difficult. Libraries mu
 st meet their campuses' needs while operating within finite budgets and p
 ursuing broader commitments to affordability\, equity\, and the long-term
  health of scholarly communication.  This panel will bring together libra
 rians with expertise in collections and acquisitions strategy\, academic 
 engagement\, and scholarly communication to explore how libraries can mak
 e spending decisions that are fiscally responsible\, responsive to local 
 needs\, and aligned with broader professional and institutional values. H
 ow can libraries serve their campuses while also helping build a more equ
 itable\, affordable\, open\, and sustainable scholarly communication syst
 em?PanelistsRachel Caldwell (https://www.linkedin.com/in/rachel-caldwell-
 947a10247/)\, Head\, Academic Engagement\, University of Massachusetts Am
 herst Libraries  Erin Gallagher (https://experts.ufl.edu/experts/erin.gal
 lagher/)\, Chair\, Acquisitions &amp\; Discovery Services\, University of
  Florida Libraries  Laura Hanscom (https://libraries.mit.edu/scholarly/ab
 out/)\, Head\, Scholarly Communications &amp\; Collections Strategy\, MIT
  Libraries  ModeratorWilla Liburd (https://libraries.indiana.edu/willa-li
 burd)\, Research Impact &amp\; Open Scholarship Librarian\, IU Bloomingto
 n Libraries
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Every subscription renewed\, publishing
  agreement signed\, infrastructure project supported\, or service discont
 inued helps shape the scholarly communication ecosystem—for better or f
 or worse.</p><p>  But making spending decisions that reflect library valu
 es is difficult. Libraries must meet their campuses' needs while operatin
 g within finite budgets and pursuing broader commitments to affordability
 \, equity\, and the long-term health of scholarly communication.</p><p>  
 This panel will bring together librarians with expertise in collections a
 nd acquisitions strategy\, academic engagement\, and scholarly communicat
 ion to explore how libraries can make spending decisions that are fiscall
 y responsible\, responsive to local needs\, and aligned with broader prof
 essional and institutional values. How can libraries serve their campuses
  while also helping build a more equitable\, affordable\, open\, and sust
 ainable scholarly communication system?</p><p><strong>Panelists</strong><
 /p><ul><li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/rachel-caldwell-947a10247
 /">Rachel Caldwell</a>\, Head\, Academic Engagement\, University of Massa
 chusetts Amherst Libraries  </li><li><a href="https://experts.ufl.edu/exp
 erts/erin.gallagher/">Erin Gallagher</a>\, Chair\, Acquisitions &amp\; Di
 scovery Services\, University of Florida Libraries  </li><li><a href="htt
 ps://libraries.mit.edu/scholarly/about/">Laura Hanscom</a>\, Head\, Schol
 arly Communications &amp\; Collections Strategy\, MIT Libraries  </li></u
 l><p><strong>Moderator</strong></p><ul><li><a href="https://libraries.ind
 iana.edu/willa-liburd" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Willa Liburd</a>\, 
 Research Impact &amp\; Open Scholarship Librarian\, IU Bloomington Librar
 ies  </li></ul>
UID:20261019T140000Z-2417427@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20260914T144704Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2417427-the-cost-of-values-what
 -should-libraries-pay-for
CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
LAST-MODIFIED:20260922T154805Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop
 /1/src_region/0,0,3200,3200/32496_oa_week_2026_livewhale.rev.1789410307.j
 pg
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2417427
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/heig
 ht/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,3200\,3200/32496_oa_week_2026_livewhale.re
 v.1789410307.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
